# RUN: llc -mtriple=amdgcn -mcpu=gfx1250 -run-pass=machineverifier -o /dev/null %s

# The 64-bit VGPR source of FPTRUNC_ROUND_F32_F64_PSEUDO must be an even-aligned
# VGPR tuple on subtargets that require aligned VGPRs: SIModeRegister lowers the
# pseudo to V_CVT_F32_F64_e32, whose source must be even-aligned. This is a
# pre-commit test: the machine verifier does not yet reject the misaligned
# odd-start physical source register below. A following change routes this
# operand through an aligned operand register class so the verifier rejects it.

---
name: fptrunc_round_f64_misaligned_src0
tracksRegLiveness: true
body: |
  bb.0:
    liveins: $vgpr1_vgpr2
    $vgpr0 = FPTRUNC_ROUND_F32_F64_PSEUDO $vgpr1_vgpr2, 1, implicit $mode, implicit $exec
    S_ENDPGM 0
...
